{
 "slug": "danube",
 "lines": [
  {
   "o": 0.443,
   "text": "You know the Danube: four capitals, ten countries. But you've never seen where part of it really goes.",
   "chunks": [
    "YOU KNOW THE *DANUBE:*",
    "*FOUR CAPITALS,*",
    "*TEN COUNTRIES.*",
    "BUT YOU'VE NEVER SEEN",
    "WHERE PART OF|IT *REALLY GOES.*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 7.243,
   "text": "It starts in Germany's Black Forest, heading for the Black Sea.",
   "chunks": [
    "IT STARTS IN GERMANY'S",
    "*BLACK FOREST,*",
    "HEADING FOR THE|*BLACK SEA.*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 10.976,
   "text": "On the way: Vienna. Then, just 56 kilometres later... Bratislava.",
   "chunks": [
    "ON THE WAY:",
    "*VIENNA.*",
    "THEN, JUST|*56 KILOMETRES* LATER...",
    "*BRATISLAVA.*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 16.043,
   "text": "Two capitals, closer than some office commutes.",
   "chunks": [
    "TWO CAPITALS,",
    "CLOSER THAN|*SOME OFFICE COMMUTES.*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 19.433,
   "text": "Then it splits Budapest in half, and runs through Belgrade.",
   "chunks": [
    "THEN IT SPLITS *BUDAPEST*",
    "IN HALF,",
    "AND RUNS THROUGH *BELGRADE.*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 23.205,
   "text": "Four capitals on one river. No river on Earth has more.",
   "chunks": [
    "*FOUR CAPITALS*",
    "ON ONE RIVER.",
    "NO RIVER ON EARTH",
    "HAS *MORE.*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 27.481,
   "text": "So why, near its start, does it sometimes... disappear?",
   "chunks": [
    "SO WHY,",
    "NEAR ITS START,",
    "DOES IT SOMETIMES...",
    "*DISAPPEAR?*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 31.738,
   "text": "Rewind. Near Immendingen, in Germany, the riverbed is limestone, full of cracks.",
   "chunks": [
    "*REWIND.*",
    "NEAR *IMMENDINGEN,* IN GERMANY,",
    "THE RIVERBED IS *LIMESTONE,*",
    "FULL OF *CRACKS.*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 37.186,
   "text": "The river leaks straight into the ground. In 1921, that stretch ran dry on 309 days.",
   "chunks": [
    "THE RIVER *LEAKS*",
    "STRAIGHT INTO THE GROUND.",
    "IN *1921,*",
    "THAT STRETCH RAN DRY",
    "ON *309 DAYS.*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 44.5,
   "text": "Rivers need days off too. Just... not 309.",
   "chunks": [
    "RIVERS NEED DAYS|OFF TOO.",
    "JUST... NOT *309.*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 47.814,
   "text": "In 1877, scientists poured salt and dye into the cracks... and waited.",
   "chunks": [
    "IN *1877,*",
    "SCIENTISTS POURED|*SALT AND DYE*",
    "INTO THE CRACKS...",
    "AND WAITED."
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 53.024,
   "text": "60 hours later, it popped up 12 kilometres south, in a spring that flows into Lake Constance.",
   "chunks": [
    "*60 HOURS* LATER,",
    "IT POPPED UP|*12 KILOMETRES* SOUTH,",
    "IN A SPRING",
    "THAT FLOWS INTO|*LAKE CONSTANCE.*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 58.767,
   "text": "Lake Constance drains into the Rhine. Which flows to the North Sea. The wrong sea.",
   "chunks": [
    "LAKE CONSTANCE DRAINS|INTO THE *RHINE.*",
    "WHICH FLOWS TO|THE *NORTH SEA.*",
    "THE *WRONG SEA.*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 63.7,
   "text": "German states even took it to court, in 1927. Over water that left on its own.",
   "chunks": [
    "GERMAN STATES EVEN|TOOK IT",
    "TO COURT,",
    "IN *1927.*",
    "OVER WATER",
    "THAT *LEFT*|*ON ITS OWN.*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 68.948,
   "text": "And the twist? Geologists think the upper Danube may one day switch to the Rhine... for good.",
   "chunks": [
    "AND THE *TWIST?*",
    "GEOLOGISTS THINK",
    "THE UPPER DANUBE",
    "MAY ONE DAY SWITCH|TO THE *RHINE...*",
    "*FOR GOOD.*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 74.576,
   "text": "Four capitals, ten countries... and a river that can't keep its own water.",
   "chunks": [
    "FOUR CAPITALS,",
    "TEN COUNTRIES...",
    "AND A RIVER",
    "THAT *CAN'T KEEP*|*ITS OWN WATER.*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 78.881,
   "text": "This is Bhoogol. Follow for more Geography Fun Facts.",
   "chunks": [
    "THIS IS *BHUGOL.*",
    "FOLLOW FOR MORE|*GEOGRAPHY FUN FACTS.*"
   ]
  }
 ],
